# Entry Main: a block of one place describes a Structure with one field, as two do (the book #structure-result: the
# form of the record decides, a block of places). D describes `return:` with `int: first`; C returns node\Solo. The
# caller receives Solo itself: the write through node\result changes D\Solo\first. Solo\first 11, observed 7.
@: result 0
int: observed 0
D:
    Solo:
        int: first 7
    end: Solo
    return:
        int: first
    end: return
    C:
        return: node\Solo
    end: C
end: D
---
Main:
    node\result := D\C()
    node\observed := node\result\first
    node\result\first := 11
